From: =?UTF-8?q?Lu=C3=ADs=20Duarte?= <lduarte@cloudflare.com>
Date: Wed, 29 Jul 2026 14:03:02 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Honour SVG view fragments on image loads (img.svg#viewname)

An SVG fragment naming a <view> element selects that view: its viewBox
(and preserveAspectRatio, when present) replace the root's for that
rendering (SVG2 linking.html#ViewElement). usvg has no fragment
handling and the fragment never reached the parse, so <img
src="views.svg#transform"> rendered the default view (WPT
view-transform-viewBox.html).

apply_svg_view_fragment rewrites the root tag string-level before the
usvg parse (find the <view> by id, lift its viewBox/PAR onto the
root) and ImageHandler carries the src fragment from load_image to
the svg fallback branch. Unmatched fragments and viewBox-less views
leave the source untouched, the spec's fallback to a normal view.
Background-image fragments (damage.rs path) are not wired; note in
the field doc.
